    "created_at": "2016-07-11T17:36:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-11T17:36:12Z",
    "body": "Worth noting that the behavior of windowProxy.top is inconsistent across browser implementations in the above scenario: it becomes null in Chrome/FF; whereas it becomes self-parented in IE: https://jsfiddle.net/6epmjr5L/7/\n\nDoes the current language of the spec actually allows the top attribute to ever be null? Is the \"otherwise\" clause meant to apply to the 'no browsing context' case?\n\n> The top IDL attribute on the Window object of a Document that has a browsing context b must return the WindowProxy object of its top-level browsing context (which would be its own WindowProxy object if it was a top-level browsing context itself), if it has one, or its own WindowProxy object otherwise (e.g. if it was a detached nested browsing context).\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
