    "created_at": "2016-07-12T20:27:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-12T20:27:45Z",
    "body": "I am trying to work through this and it's quite messy.\n\nFirst, I think we can certainly clarify things as suggested by @Ms2ger in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/1180, by making \"nested browsing context\" an explicit field of all \"browsing context containers\", and setting it to null in certain situations.\n\nFor top/parent/frameElement, however, browsers seem to diverge a lot ([test case](http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=4317))\n- Firefox/Chrome return null for top/parent/frameElement\n- Edge seems to error violently with \"Object expected\" when you try to do anything with the `iframeWindow`.\n- Safari TP seems to make all properties of `iframeWindow` undefined, including even document.\n\nI would like to try to specify the Firefox/Chrome behavior. My current thoughts on how to do this are:\n- Do _not_ have a strong reference from WindowProxy to the browsing context.\n  - In top/parent/frameElement, check to see if there exists a browsing context for this Window object. If not, return null.\n  - Otherwise, proceed as in the existing algorithms.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
